title: APC InRow Cooling Devices: Temperature
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/environment/apc
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 The current temperature of all sensors in an InRow Cooling device.

 You can configure upper levels for {WARN}/{CRIT} (default: 30, 35).

 The service goes {WARN}/{CRIT} if the temperature is higher than these levels.

 This check uses the PowerNet-MIB. It reads the airIRRC objects of older
 InRow units as well as the generic cooling unit status tables of newer
 units (e.g. InRow ACRC301S), which do not provide the airIRRC objects
 anymore.

item:
 The name of the sensor, e.g. Rack Inlet, Supply Air, Return Air, Entering Fluid,
 Leaving Fluid. Newer units report the sensor names of their status tables, e.g.
 Rack Inlet 1, Unit Maximum Rack Inlet, Entering Chilled Water.

discovery:
 One service is created for each temperature sensor.
